invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20_vector.c
catches: chacha20_equiv_test
reason: the last pass XORs only whole 16-byte rows, the way a vector loop
  that forgets its remainder does, so the last 1 to 15 bytes of any
  length that is not a multiple of 16 pass through unencrypted. CBMC
  cannot read an intrinsic, so no proof covers this file, and
  bin/chacha20_equiv_test is what holds it to chacha20.c: its
  every-length pass runs each length from 0 to 2,048 bytes.

--- old
        if (whole < n) {
--- new
        if (whole > n) {
